--TEST--
a `|>` whose right side is a method reference is refused, and the note names PHP 8.5's operator — `rule:expressions/pipeline-hole-once`'s E0129
--FILE--
<?nvs
// rule:expressions/pipeline-substitution — this `|>` substitutes a hole where
// PHP 8.5's applies a callable, so the habit is caught at the character where
// it goes wrong rather than meaning something else.
string $padded = "  x  ";
echo $padded |> Core\Str::trim(...), "\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0129]: the right side of `|>` needs the hole `$_`
%A= note: PHP 8.5's `|>` applies a callable; Novis's substitutes `$_` at compile time
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
